cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Not Evidence: twelve signals that look like evidence and aren't"
message: >-
  If you cite this, please cite the entry and its specimen rather than the
  repository alone. Each pattern states a claim and each specimen records the
  measurement behind it, and several entries argue something different from what
  they set out to argue — so which version you read matters. Every entry carries
  a status and every specimen an adjudication.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lange
    given-names: Jon
    alias: jon-lange
repository-code: "https://github.com/jon-lange/not-evidence"
url: "https://jon-lange.github.io/not-evidence/"
abstract: >-
  A bounded catalogue of twelve signals that are routinely accepted as evidence
  and are not — a guardrail that refused the obvious attack, a green test that
  never ran, a judge that shares the subject's lineage, a label that says
  sanitized — each paired with the refusal that closes it and a runnable
  specimen that tests whether the claim survives contact with something that can
  contradict it. Ten of the twelve entries were revised by their own specimens
  and five had their central claim fail. No figure appears that was not
  generated in the repository itself.
keywords:
  - llm-evaluation
  - prompt-injection
  - guardrails
  - mutation-testing
  - llm-as-judge
  - re-identification
  - software-patterns
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/jon-lange/not-evidence/blob/main/LICENSE"
date-released: "2026-08-06"
